[agent] I'm giving up cleanly — the platform had no compute available for the entire run, so the deliverable could not be created.
[agent] ## What happened
[agent] **The deliverable does not exist.** The table `workspace.mlpab8d9f43.recs971bf6` was never created because no Databricks compute would start during the whole task window.
[agent] **What succeeded:**
[agent] - Created the UC volume `workspace.mlpab8d9f43.raw` and uploaded all three input CSVs to `/Volumes/workspace/mlpab8d9f43/raw/` via `databricks fs cp`.
[agent] - Fully prepared the platform-side work: a `CREATE TABLE` statement (rec_id STRING primary key, user_id, rank INT, item_id, with change data feed enabled) and an `INSERT` that computes the 8-dim dot product for every user × item pair via `read_files` on the volume CSVs, anti-joins out already-interacted items, and takes `row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY score DESC, item_id ASC) <= 5` — plus an `online-tables create` spec (`recs971bf6_online`) for the low-latency copy.
[agent] **What blocked it (environment, not a missing CLI capability):**
[agent] 1. Both SQL warehouses (`Serverless Starter Warehouse` and `mlpab-grader`) stayed in `STARTING` for ~60 minutes with a persistent health error: `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED: Cannot create the resource, please try again later.` My queued SQL statements sat in `PENDING` until the warehouses auto-stopped, at which point the statement failed with "warehouse … was stopped." Late resubmissions hung and the resource exhaustion never cleared.
[agent] 2. The fallback compute path — a one-time serverless job run of a notebook doing the same SQL (notebook was imported to `/Users/benedict@hopsworks.ai/mlpab8d9f43/build_recs`) — was rejected with: `Triggering new runs for organization 7474656148089623 is currently disabled temporarily.`
[agent] The `databricks` CLI itself had every capability needed (statement execution API, `online-tables create`, `fs cp`, `volumes create`); the workspace simply had zero available compute capacity and job triggering disabled, so no ingestion/transformation could run on the platform.
